IMO, that's 2 major changes you could make to your game to increase
your ascension ratio.

Certainly with an un-ID'd cloak you might want to try to ID it before
wishing, but never go onto an explored level to do so.  If you're
running back to a stashed scroll of ID, fine.  If you're moving forward
with no known close source, get the MR _now_.  Eliminating instadeaths
as soon as you can is the key to ascending at a high ratio.

2nd, SDSM is a poor wish at that point; you have a 75% chance of
getting reflection before the Quest/Castle without a wish and without
random luck.  You have a 0% chance of getting MR with the same
constraints.  Of course, wizard bones can give MR, but even if you had
an 75% chance of finding them (highly unlikely even on a crowded public
server), MR is so much more valuable than reflection that it's still
worth the wish preference.



